// Three probes without an answer: at +0.2, then +0.4 and +0.8 after the one before, each with the clock's value
// then, and the fourth expiry, 1.6 s after the third probe, finds three unanswered and ends the connection; read
// reports ETIMEDOUT then. Linux counts unanswered probes against tcp_retries2 too, but sends them only while it holds
// unsent data; see the TCP page.
--tcp_data_retries=3
0 socket(..., SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP) = 3
+0 bind(3, ..., ...) = 0
+0 listen(3, 1) = 0

+0 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 46720 <mss 1460,nop,nop,TS val 0 ecr 100>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0 accept(3, ..., ...) = 4

+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 0 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0.2 > . 0:0(0) ack 1 win 46720 <nop,nop,TS val 200 ecr 100>
+0.4 > . 0:0(0) ack 1 win 46720 <nop,nop,TS val 600 ecr 100>
+0.8 > . 0:0(0) ack 1 win 46720 <nop,nop,TS val 1400 ecr 100>
+1.6~+1.61 read(4, ..., 1) = -1 ETIMEDOUT
